1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,660
ClearShelf: allergen clearance and

2
00:00:02,680 --> 00:00:04,770
recall watch for online grocers.

3
00:00:05,717 --> 00:00:07,427
A solo entry from Singapore.

4
00:00:08,567 --> 00:00:11,747
Open Food Facts tags these Plant-Based Puffs as vegan.

5
00:00:12,347 --> 00:00:16,067
The FDA says they tested positive for milk.

6
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:18,767
An online grocer's compliance officer must

7
00:00:18,787 --> 00:00:21,137
catch that before the listing goes live.

8
00:00:24,662 --> 00:00:27,692
The officer pastes a barcode and picks the UK.

9
00:00:30,450 --> 00:00:33,470
Each step streams as the local Nemotron model plans it:

10
00:00:33,750 --> 00:00:35,590
the product row, the recall notice,

11
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,350
the data-quality gate, memory.

12
00:00:37,950 --> 00:00:40,040
Every read goes through Zetaris.

13
00:00:42,833 --> 00:00:45,073
In Zetaris, each product is a live REST

14
00:00:45,093 --> 00:00:49,593
table beside the openFDA and FSA feeds,

15
00:00:49,973 --> 00:00:52,733
and the clearance_usl semantic layer joins

16
00:00:52,753 --> 00:00:55,043
them with keys and data-quality rules.

17
00:01:04,533 --> 00:01:06,593
The result: HOLD, applied automatically,

18
00:01:06,613 --> 00:01:08,373
since holding needs no signature.

19
00:01:08,953 --> 00:01:12,753
Each chip opens its evidence: the exact Lightning SQL,

20
00:01:12,953 --> 00:01:15,943
the source, the licence and the cache time.

21
00:01:19,267 --> 00:01:20,047
Why was this held?

22
00:01:20,387 --> 00:01:23,707
Five plain lines: the recall, the missing ingredient list,

23
00:01:23,887 --> 00:01:25,767
and the vegan claim that milk contradicts,

24
00:01:26,087 --> 00:01:27,357
each with its evidence.

25
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:30,900
On this dark chocolate, a keyword rule reads milk in

26
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:33,800
cocoa butter and treats "may contain" as "contains".

27
00:01:34,600 --> 00:01:38,330
Nemotron names no allergen there, and a verifier must agree.

28
00:01:39,367 --> 00:01:41,067
Clearing always needs the officer:

29
00:01:41,647 --> 00:01:43,187
the form shows what will be signed,

30
00:01:43,547 --> 00:01:45,667
the server issues a single-use contract,

31
00:01:45,907 --> 00:01:48,117
and only then is the decision written.

32
00:01:53,533 --> 00:01:56,083
Zetaris reads the signed row straight back.

33
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:59,853
The recall watch can replay a known past:

34
00:01:59,873 --> 00:02:03,393
as of 10 October it sees only notices reported by then,

35
00:02:03,573 --> 00:02:05,017
and a banner says so.

36
00:02:05,067 --> 00:02:07,547
Polling to today, new notices arrive and

37
00:02:07,567 --> 00:02:09,187
a bounded investigation runs:

38
00:02:09,707 --> 00:02:12,347
each Markovian step carries a small state forward,

39
00:02:12,547 --> 00:02:14,217
so the prompt stays flat.

40
00:02:15,933 --> 00:02:19,113
An FDA notice names this cake's barcode exactly.

41
00:02:19,773 --> 00:02:21,233
It's a US-only recall,

42
00:02:21,493 --> 00:02:24,913
so the UK listing is held automatically, with the reason.

43
00:02:25,533 --> 00:02:27,663
Name-only matches wait for a person.

44
00:02:28,233 --> 00:02:31,533
Contradictions are queued, never settled by the last write.

45
00:02:32,033 --> 00:02:34,553
The officer resolves the milk conflict with a reason,

46
00:02:34,573 --> 00:02:36,883
and the ledger records who decided.

47
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:43,680
The footer shows a Ritz cracker re-check

48
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:45,680
reusing its verified extraction:

49
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:53,110
tool tokens fall from 3,658 to 804, and 61 seconds to 48.

50
00:02:54,400 --> 00:02:58,840
Zetaris is the only data path, and its SQL is the citation.

51
00:02:59,580 --> 00:03:02,620
Meterless engines run the loop, the memory and the world model;

52
00:03:03,020 --> 00:03:05,440
the signed contracts follow Meterless Scout's spec.

53
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:08,470
Nemotron runs on one local GPU.

54
00:03:10,433 --> 00:03:12,573
Measured: ten of ten scenarios pass,

55
00:03:13,233 --> 00:03:18,053
label precision is 1.00 against 0.71 for keywords,

56
00:03:18,453 --> 00:03:20,123
and nothing clears unsigned.

57
00:03:21,600 --> 00:03:22,240
ClearShelf.

58
00:03:22,600 --> 00:03:25,610
Every decision is cited, and every release is signed.
